    "narration": {
      "1": "Everything starts with a shopper on the web…",
      "2": "…or in the mobile app.",
      "3": "The edge: CDN and load balancer.",
      "4": "The CDN serves the storefront and every image from the edge.",
      "5": "The load balancer takes API traffic and drops unhealthy gateway pods.",
      "6": "The storefront is a single-page app; it talks to the same API as mobile.",
      "7": "The API gateway authenticates, rate-limits and routes every call.",
      "8": "Six services run in one Kubernetes namespace.",
      "9": "Identity owns accounts, sessions and tokens.",
      "10": "Catalog serves products, prices and availability.",
      "11": "Search answers queries from its own index.",
      "12": "Cart keeps baskets in the session cache.",
      "13": "Checkout is the money path: click it to see its own steps.",
      "14": "Inventory reserves stock while the payment runs.",
      "15": "Each service owns its data store.",
      "16": "Users DB: PostgreSQL.",
      "17": "Catalog DB: PostgreSQL, read replicas behind it.",
      "18": "The search index: OpenSearch.",
      "19": "The session cache: Redis.",
      "20": "Orders DB is the system of record for every order.",
      "21": "Payments charges the card…",
      "22": "…through Stripe. When Stripe slows down, Payments and Checkout feel it first.",
      "23": "Checkout publishes order.placed on the event bus.",
      "24": "Workers react to events, after the shopper has gone.",
      "25": "Fulfilment picks orders and books couriers.",
      "26": "Notifications sends the confirmation email…",
      "27": "…through the email provider."
    }
  }
